[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186105745 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/id #uuid "125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-20959" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9bddf8b0-a60d-5d3f-b177-ef56758827de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9bddf8b0-a60d-5d3f-b177-ef56758827de" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bddf8b0-a60d-5d3f-b177-ef56758827de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7d1e9298-04d9-5141-818c-3600950452a4" "answer-adbb2e17-3aaa-5c1e-9d3b-42764e417a7c" "answer-15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" "answer-a15c2e45-6e4f-5f3f-a77c-905430031175" "answer-3ea4d3db-3e0f-5246-9e9e-4b07b0cfdfa3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d1e9298-04d9-5141-818c-3600950452a4" :answer/id #uuid "7d1e9298-04d9-5141-818c-3600950452a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adbb2e17-3aaa-5c1e-9d3b-42764e417a7c" :answer/id #uuid "adbb2e17-3aaa-5c1e-9d3b-42764e417a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" :answer/id #uuid "15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a15c2e45-6e4f-5f3f-a77c-905430031175" :answer/id #uuid "a15c2e45-6e4f-5f3f-a77c-905430031175" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ea4d3db-3e0f-5246-9e9e-4b07b0cfdfa3" :answer/id #uuid "3ea4d3db-3e0f-5246-9e9e-4b07b0cfdfa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105746 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-897c434c-2b3e-570b-8210-f27b51719e55"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-897c434c-2b3e-570b-8210-f27b51719e55" :question/id #uuid "897c434c-2b3e-570b-8210-f27b51719e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-20964" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=0 \\\\ 2x-10y=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=0 \\\\ 0x+0y=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=3$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=3,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e2c1a1e-5d57-5327-abb7-fcc53ab8ec5f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e2c1a1e-5d57-5327-abb7-fcc53ab8ec5f" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e2c1a1e-5d57-5327-abb7-fcc53ab8ec5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c9ed7e74-cd82-5c17-8e1e-7e850dab4062" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5ac4430-b766-5ef0-94db-838c49da75cf" "answer-75926ae1-f71f-5fca-920d-fc96549abf2a" "answer-e6c2949c-d93d-5056-afd3-68aaf8051b1c" "answer-202e7707-594c-5dc6-b642-d0f2a066b531" "answer-c9ed7e74-cd82-5c17-8e1e-7e850dab4062"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5ac4430-b766-5ef0-94db-838c49da75cf" :answer/id #uuid "b5ac4430-b766-5ef0-94db-838c49da75cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75926ae1-f71f-5fca-920d-fc96549abf2a" :answer/id #uuid "75926ae1-f71f-5fca-920d-fc96549abf2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6c2949c-d93d-5056-afd3-68aaf8051b1c" :answer/id #uuid "e6c2949c-d93d-5056-afd3-68aaf8051b1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-202e7707-594c-5dc6-b642-d0f2a066b531" :answer/id #uuid "202e7707-594c-5dc6-b642-d0f2a066b531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9ed7e74-cd82-5c17-8e1e-7e850dab4062" :answer/id #uuid "c9ed7e74-cd82-5c17-8e1e-7e850dab4062" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186107080 :tutorial/content "Let's consider a system of linear equations where the corresponding coefficient matrix is singular. For example, consider the following system and its associated augmented matrix:\n![](images/6a/6a69daf7712312876b0ec97c540bbc472e46a7938beb8a59e694a04ad0b1d8c6.svg)\n\nTo solve the system, we can reduce $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as usual. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/a8/a8bfe3f6b27247ee9b27db8346fd94fb9068c85dec6f4a71517a821dee48dbf3.svg)\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 2y = -5.\n$$\n\nFinally, we describe the **general solution** of our system.\n\n- The first variable in our equation, $x,$ is called a **basic variable**.\n\n- The second variable in our equation, $y,$ is called a **free variable**.\n\nSolving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x = -5+2y.$ So the general solution of the system is\n![](images/0b/0ba4a232f29dd6fce2a8f6d7cda39b4f5b192c20fc91fe4403dfe648231382c5.svg)\nwhere the free variable $y$ is any number.\n\nIn vector form, this solution is written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that this is the equation of a straight line on a plane. Any point on this line satisfies our system of equations.\n\nIf we want to find some **particular solution** of the system, we simply choose some particular value of $y$ and find the corresponding value of $x$ on the line. For example, if we choose $y=0,$ then the corresponding value is $x=-5$ and the particular solution is $x=-5,$ $y=0.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186107097 :tutorial/content "Sometimes, a system of equations might not have any solutions. For example, consider the following augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is\n![](images/e8/e8c64d8be247afd3e8ab02abc69e33635ef0234dbcbbc60f42379021a39a58a2.svg)\n\nThe final equation, $0x+0y=10,$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=10,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/id #uuid "125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed"] ["question-125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-20959"] ["question-125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] ["question-125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-9bddf8b0-a60d-5d3f-b177-ef56758827de" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bddf8b0-a60d-5d3f-b177-ef56758827de"] ["answer-7d1e9298-04d9-5141-818c-3600950452a4" :answer/id #uuid "7d1e9298-04d9-5141-818c-3600950452a4"] ["answer-7d1e9298-04d9-5141-818c-3600950452a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7d1e9298-04d9-5141-818c-3600950452a4" :answer/value "⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-adbb2e17-3aaa-5c1e-9d3b-42764e417a7c" :answer/id #uuid "adbb2e17-3aaa-5c1e-9d3b-42764e417a7c"] ["answer-adbb2e17-3aaa-5c1e-9d3b-42764e417a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-adbb2e17-3aaa-5c1e-9d3b-42764e417a7c" :answer/value "⟨-2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" :answer/id #uuid "15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2"] ["answer-15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" :answer/value "⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty 